# Sign in with your Python client

Install Python 3.11 or newer and Chrome or Chromium. From the directory containing
this README, run the first command to install the Python dependency. The second
command opens the website in its own temporary browser.

```sh
python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python3 client.py login
```

Sign in and complete MFA in the browser. Once you see the intended dashboard,
return to the terminal and press Enter. The command closes its browser and prints
`{"authentication": "user-confirmed", "sessionClosed": true}`. It exits zero.
If the site uses a separate starting path, pass its HTTPS login URL with
`--url`. Use `--browser chromium` for Chromium or `--browser-path` to specify
the installed executable. Cancel with Ctrl+C and retry from a fresh terminal if
sign-in is interrupted.

This version provides login only. From Python, `with client.login() as session:`
keeps the signed-in browser open for the duration of the block. Each invocation
starts fresh. The generated directory contains no passwords or cookies.
